msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2054
msgid "After you trust net area. Add 5–15% (more for patterns), then convert to the seller’s unit if needed and round up to packaging."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1956
msgid "Age, birthdays, and why they diverge"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1380
msgid "Air-fryers and toaster ovens have different thermal mass. Treat their charts as separate; still convert units carefully when a recipe only lists one scale."
msgstr "ノンフライヤーとオーブントースターでは熱質量が異なります。それらのチャートを別のものとして扱います。レシピに 1 つのスケールしか記載されていない場合でも、単位は慎重に変換してください。"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2169
msgid "Airline baggage is kilograms or pounds—not stone. Never put stone on a shipping label."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1600
msgid "Airlines often market 23 kg as “50 lb,” but 23 kg is about 50.71 lb. Pack below the kilogram limit after converting with an exact factor, and leave a buffer for scale differences."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2224
msgid "Airspeed is a speed—with extra labels"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2214
msgid "Airspeed Units Explained"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2234
msgid "Airspeeds and ATIS winds are typically in knots. One knot = 1.852 km/h = about 1.15078 mph. When a POH lists V-speeds in knots, convert for a passenger explanation if you want—but memorize and fly the knot values you trained with."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:375
msgid "Alcohol and extracts in teaspoons look trivial until you scale cocktails or flavourings for a crowd. Convert to millilitres, scale, then portion with a jug or syringe for consistency."
msgstr "大勢でカクテルやフレーバーを量るまでは、ティースプーンに入ったアルコールやエキスは取るに足らないものに見えます。ミリリットルに換算し、秤量してから、水差しまたは注射器で一定量に分けます。"

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2267
msgid "Align chart distance units with speed units before ETA math. Verify tablet app unit settings before navigation practice."
msgstr ""

